The File-Configurations request returns a tagged, nonempty list of per-mode
configurations. File keeps returning the legacy list of directives.

  $ make_dune_project 3.16
  $ cat > dune <<'EOF'
  > (library (name example) (flags ()))
  > EOF
  $ touch example.ml example.mli
  $ dune build @check
  $ ocamlc_where="$(ocamlc -where)"
  $ export BUILD_PATH_PREFIX_MAP="/OCAMLC_WHERE=$ocamlc_where:$BUILD_PATH_PREFIX_MAP"

The complete response includes the compilation mode, default flag, source kind,
counterpart and Merlin directives, using the same schema as Merlin's decoder.

  $ query_ocaml_merlin_configurations_pp example.ml | tee implementation.out
  (CONFIGURATIONS
   ((CONFIG
     (MODE ocaml)
     (DEFAULT true)
     (KIND implementation)
     (COUNTERPART $TESTCASE_ROOT/example.mli)
     (DIRECTIVES
      ((INDEX $TESTCASE_ROOT/_build/default/.example.objs/cctx.ocaml-index)
       (STDLIB /OCAMLC_WHERE)
       (SOURCE_ROOT $TESTCASE_ROOT)
       (EXCLUDE_QUERY_DIR)
       (B $TESTCASE_ROOT/_build/default/.example.objs/byte)
       (S $TESTCASE_ROOT)
       (FLG (-g))
       (UNIT_NAME example))))))

Absolute source paths and build paths select the same configuration.

  $ for file in "$PWD/example.ml" _build/default/example.ml; do
  >   query_ocaml_merlin_configurations_pp "$file" | diff implementation.out -
  > done

The interface has the same directives but its own source kind and counterpart.

  $ sed -e 's/KIND implementation/KIND interface/' \
  >   -e 's#example.mli)#example.ml)#' implementation.out > interface.out
  $ query_ocaml_merlin_configurations_pp example.mli | diff interface.out -

The legacy directives are unchanged. Wrapping them in the new envelope gives
exactly the same canonical S-expression as the plural request.

  $ query_ocaml_merlin_pp example.ml > directives
  $ {
  >   printf '%s\n' '(CONFIGURATIONS ((CONFIG (MODE ocaml) (DEFAULT true)'
  >   printf '(KIND implementation) (COUNTERPART "%s/example.mli") (DIRECTIVES\n' "$PWD"
  >   cat directives
  >   printf '))))\n'
  > } > expected.sexp
  $ dune internal sexp-to-csexp < expected.sexp > expected.csexp
  $ query_ocaml_merlin_configurations example.ml | diff expected.csexp -

Lookup failures are tagged, not successful empty configurations. A filename
without an extension is ambiguous when both source kinds exist; legacy File
still permits that fallback.

  $ query_ocaml_merlin_configurations_pp missing.ml
  (CONFIGURATIONS-ERROR "No config found for file missing.ml. Try calling 'dune build'.")
  $ query_ocaml_merlin_configurations_pp example
  (CONFIGURATIONS-ERROR "No config found for file example. Try calling 'dune build'.")
  $ query_ocaml_merlin_pp example | diff directives -
  $ query_ocaml_merlin_configurations_pp ../outside.ml
  (CONFIGURATIONS-ERROR "path outside the workspace: ../outside.ml from .")

Requests can be interleaved on the same connection. Lookup failures and unknown
commands do not end the session; Halt does.

  $ cat > requests <<'EOF'
  > (File-Configurations missing.ml)
  > (File missing.ml)
  > (File-Configurations)
  > (File-Configurations example.mli)
  > (File example.ml)
  > Halt
  > (File-Configurations missing.ml)
  > EOF
  $ dune internal sexp-to-csexp < requests > requests.csexp
  $ dune ocaml-merlin < requests.csexp > responses.csexp
  $ dune internal sexp-pp --format=csexp responses.csexp \
  >   | grep -E 'CONFIGURATIONS|ERROR|MODE|DEFAULT|KIND|UNIT_NAME'
  (CONFIGURATIONS-ERROR "No config found for file missing.ml. Try calling 'dune build'.")
  ((ERROR "No config found for file missing.ml. Try calling 'dune build'."))
  ((ERROR "Bad input: (File-Configurations)"))
  (CONFIGURATIONS
     (MODE ocaml)
     (DEFAULT true)
     (KIND interface)
       (UNIT_NAME example))))))
   (UNIT_NAME example))

An unreadable configuration also returns a tagged error, without changing the
legacy error response.

  $ chmod u+w _build/default/.merlin-conf/lib-example
  $ printf invalid > _build/default/.merlin-conf/lib-example
  $ query_ocaml_merlin_configurations_pp example.ml
  (CONFIGURATIONS-ERROR "The current Merlin configuration has been generated by another, incompatible, version of Dune. Please rebuild the project. (Using the same version of Dune as the one running the 'ocaml-merlin' server.)")
  $ query_ocaml_merlin_pp example.ml
  ((ERROR "The current Merlin configuration has been generated by another, incompatible, version of Dune. Please rebuild the project. (Using the same version of Dune as the one running the 'ocaml-merlin' server.)"))
